### Telemetry: provision a device, ingest a batch (idempotent), read the series, excursions
### Mirrors tests/integration/test_telemetry_*.py. See docs/TELEMETRY.md for the data path.
### Send top to bottom.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000

### Admin login
# @name adminLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@aurora-clinic.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### A clinic to attach the device to
# @name clinics
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/clinics?limit=1
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.access_token}}

### Provision a device — the response includes the one-time device secret. Save it.
# @name provision
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/devices
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "clinic_id": "{{clinics.response.body.data.0.id}}",
  "location_label": "Vaccine fridge A",
  "hardware_version": "pi-zero-2w",
  "firmware_version": "1.0.0"
}

### Set a threshold policy for the device (safe band 2–8 °C, 15 min dwell, 10 min recovery)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/threshold-policies
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "device_id": "{{provision.response.body.device.id}}",
  "min_temperature_c": 2,
  "max_temperature_c": 8,
  "dwell_minutes": 15,
  "recovery_minutes": 10
}

### Ingest a batch — authenticated with the DEVICE secret, not a user token.
### Only measured_at and temperature_c are required per reading. Expect 200 with a per-item result array.
# @name batch
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/devices/{{provision.response.body.device.id}}/telemetry:batch
X-Device-Secret: {{provision.response.body.secret}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "idempotency_key": "batch-0001",
  "v": 2,
  "readings": [
    { "sequence": 1, "reading": { "measured_at": "2026-09-28T08:00:00Z", "temperature_c": 4.3, "humidity_pct": 45 } },
    { "sequence": 2, "reading": { "measured_at": "2026-09-28T08:05:00Z", "temperature_c": 4.4, "humidity_pct": 45 } }
  ]
}

### Replay the SAME batch — idempotent. Duplicates are dropped by (device_id, sequence);
### the result reports them as duplicates, not errors, and no rows are added.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/devices/{{provision.response.body.device.id}}/telemetry:batch
X-Device-Secret: {{provision.response.body.secret}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "idempotency_key": "batch-0001",
  "v": 2,
  "readings": [
    { "sequence": 1, "reading": { "measured_at": "2026-09-28T08:00:00Z", "temperature_c": 4.3, "humidity_pct": 45 } },
    { "sequence": 2, "reading": { "measured_at": "2026-09-28T08:05:00Z", "temperature_c": 4.4, "humidity_pct": 45 } }
  ]
}

### A reading from the future is rejected (per-item) — a broken device clock, not real data.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/devices/{{provision.response.body.device.id}}/telemetry:batch
X-Device-Secret: {{provision.response.body.secret}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "idempotency_key": "batch-future",
  "v": 2,
  "readings": [
    { "sequence": 99, "reading": { "measured_at": "2099-01-01T00:00:00Z", "temperature_c": 4.5 } }
  ]
}

### Wrong secret — expect 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/devices/{{provision.response.body.device.id}}/telemetry:batch
X-Device-Secret: not-the-secret
Content-Type: application/json

{ "v": 2, "readings": [] }

### Read the time series, bucketed and aggregated
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/devices/{{provision.response.body.device.id}}/telemetry?bucket=5m&agg=avg
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.access_token}}

### Device health (last seen, buffer/series state)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/devices/{{provision.response.body.device.id}}/health
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.access_token}}

### Open excursions for the device (none, if the readings stayed in band)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/devices/{{provision.response.body.device.id}}/excursions?open_only=true
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.access_token}}

### Live stream (Server-Sent Events). Supports Last-Event-ID resume.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/streams/telemetry
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.access_token}}
Accept: text/event-stream
